# CITATION.cff — Citation File Format 1.2.0
# 'license:' uses the official SPDX identifier CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0, which IS on the
# SPDX License List (unlike the PolyForm licenses used by Onibex code repositories),
# so it can be declared directly. Validate before committing:
#     pipx run cffconvert --validate
# Keep 'version' and 'date-released' in sync with the GitHub Release tag: update
# both in the commit that precedes each release tag.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this documentation, please cite it as below."
title: "Onibex eCommerce 360° Documentation — ALE/IDoc configuration guides for SAP ERP and FAQ (English/Spanish)"
abstract: >-
  Bilingual (English and Spanish) technical documentation of Onibex eCommerce 360°,
  the B2B/B2C eCommerce platform designed for use with SAP ERP. It covers the
  configuration in SAP ERP through ALE and IDocs (logical systems, RFC destinations,
  IDoc ports, partner profiles, change pointers; MATMAS and DEBMAS master-data IDocs;
  ORDERS, ORDRSP, DESADV and INVOIC sales-document IDocs; custom quotation, contract
  confirmation and transport IDocs), the SICF web services used for real-time price
  and inventory queries, cross-selling configuration, credit-block reasons, the
  complete list of custom objects created in SAP ERP, and FAQ articles for the store
  administration panel.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Onibex, LLC"
    website: "https://www.onibex.com"
